### Test 1: Create a New Booking Inquiry (As Customer)
# Replace the Authorization header with a valid Customer token
# Replace vendor_id with a real vendor ID from your database seed
POST http://localhost:5430/v1/bookings
Authorization: Bearer CUSTOMER_TEST_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vendor_id": "01GD2V9BYGW9NNEXG5X9YYYYYY",
  "event_date": "2026-11-15",
  "event_type": "wedding",
  "guest_count": 250,
  "total_amount": 7500000,
  "notes": "Looking for outdoor floral setup at Chhattarpur Farms."
}

### Test 2: Vendor Accepts the Booking Request
# Replace the ':id' path variable with the actual booking ULID returned from Test 1
# Replace the Authorization header with a valid Vendor token
PATCH http://localhost:5430/v1/bookings/01KWPN94RA1FDBXHDWC62ZAHRE/accept
Authorization: Bearer VENDOR_TEST_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json